            "result_text": "Created `/app/filter.py` with the following capabilities:\n\n**What it removes:**\n- `<script>` tags and all their content\n- Event handler attributes (`onclick`, `onload`, `onerror`, etc.)\n- `javascript:` protocol in URLs\n\n**What it preserves:**\n- All HTML structure (tables, headers, divs, etc.)\n- Legitimate HTML attributes (class, id, data-*, style, etc.)\n- Formatting and whitespace exactly as-is\n- Non-dangerous content\n\nThe script reads the HTML file, processes it with regex patterns to surgically remove XSS vectors, and writes the cleaned content back in-place. Usage: `python filter.py <html_file>`"
